{"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","title":"HTTPDestinations","role":"collection","externalID":"HTTPDestinations","modules":[{"name":"HTTPDestinations"}],"roleHeading":"Framework"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"},"abstract":[{"text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" is a destination that posts each batch it receives as the requests its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" splits it into: one request for an endpoint without limits. Each body is whatever"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the encoder writes for its records, so events need no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance and the wire format is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"yours. It sends with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"type":"text","text":" through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/URLSessionTransport"},{"type":"text","text":" by default, or through any "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport"},{"type":"text","text":" you pass."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A send that gets no response, or a 5xx, 408 or 429 status, is sent again after the next wait of its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":": nominally 1 second, doubling up to 60 seconds, unless you pass another. So","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is one answered with a status the encoder lists in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder\/transientStatuses","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", which every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoder declares: empty for most servers, or each other failure its vendor answers to a request","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"worth sending again, such as Aptabase’s 418 for a slow upload.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A 2xx counts as delivered unless the encoder’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder\/outcome(of:for:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" reads its body and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"says otherwise. Some vendors answer 200 to a request they didn’t store, and say so only in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"body: Mixpanel’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"{\"status\": 0}","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or Aptabase’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"{\"error\": ...}","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for an unknown key. A 2xx the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoder reads as ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome\/rejected(reason:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is dropped and reported as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport\/rejectedInBody(status:reason:recordIDs:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". One it reads as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome\/transient(reason:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is sent again under the same backoff and deadline as a 5xx.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"An encoder should count an empty body, or one it can’t read, as delivered, so an answer it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"doesn’t recognize never sends a request again and again; the DestinationTesting conformance kit","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"checks that it does. A transient answer is retried until the request’s deadline, so an encoder","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose requests have none should return rejected instead.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each wait has full jitter by default: a random wait shorter than the nominal one, so apps refused"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at the same moment retry at different moments. Pass "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/Jitter-swift.enum\/none","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nominal waits. In tests, pass a seeded generator as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"randomNumberGenerator:"},{"type":"text","text":" for jittered waits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that repeat from one run to the next, as long as one request retries at a time: copies of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination retrying at once share the generator’s draws in the order they ask for them. Never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"seed it in production, where every device would then wait the same, which defeats the jitter. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination takes the next batch only once this one is delivered or dropped, so a tracker’s store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keeps the batch’s records until then. A batch the endpoint answers with any other status, whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request can never be sent, or that the encoder can’t encode is dropped, logged and reported on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/dropReports","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" as an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", as is each record the encoder leaves out"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of its requests. So is a request still undelivered at its "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedRequest\/deadline","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder sets for a vendor that misdates or ignores old events: the destination checks it on its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"now:"},{"type":"text","text":" clock before every attempt and sends nothing more once it has passed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tracing instrument injects the trace context of each request’s first record into its header"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fields, and "},{"code":"Content-Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is always the encoder’s."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reach for this module to send to a server whose format you write yourself. For TraffluentCollector’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"format, give the destination a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"); for PostHog,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"make it with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.postHog(projectToken:host:plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"); for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Amplitude, with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AmplitudeEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"); for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel, with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":");"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for Segment, RudderStack or Customer.io Data Pipelines, with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.segment(writeKey:region:plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":" or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentSpecEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"); for Google Analytics 4, from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"server, with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"); for Snowplow, with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SnowplowEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"); for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"TelemetryDeck, with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.telemetryDeck(appID:namespace:testMode:plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeckEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"); for Matomo, with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.matomo(url:siteID:dimensions:category:plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MatomoEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"); for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Heap, with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.heap(appID:region:plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HeapEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"); for Aptabase, with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.aptabase(appKey:host:isDebug:plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AptabaseEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"). To read events"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inside the app or in a test, use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"InMemoryDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Destinations"},{"type":"text","text":") instead."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import HTTPDestinations","","struct PlansEncoder: BatchEncoder {","    static let transientStatuses: Set<TransientStatus> = []","","    static func outcome(of response: HTTPTransportResponse, for request: EncodedRequest) -> ResponseOutcome {","        .delivered","    }","","    func requests(for batch: [EventRecord]) -> BatchRequests<Never> {","        let plans = batch.compactMap { ($0.event as? SignedUp)?.plan }","        let body = EncodedBatch(body: Data(plans.joined(separator: \"\\n\").utf8), contentType: \"text\/plain\")","        return BatchRequests(requests: [EncodedRequest(body: body, recordIDs: batch.map(\\.id))], skippedRecords: [])","    }","}","","let server = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: endpointURL,","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(token)\"],","    encoder: PlansEncoder(),","    backoff: try ExponentialBackoff(initialDelay: .seconds(2), maximumDelay: .seconds(120)))","let drops = server.dropReports","let watching = Task {","    for await drop in drops {","        print(\"Dropped a batch: \\(drop)\")","    }","}","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: server)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers this destination beside the others, and what a delivery does while a batch is retried.","type":"text"}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-batches","title":"Sending batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport"]},{"anchor":"Encoding-a-batch","title":"Encoding a batch","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch"]},{"anchor":"Reading-a-2xx-answer","title":"Reading a 2xx answer","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransportResponse"]},{"anchor":"Splitting-a-batch-into-requests","title":"Splitting a batch into requests","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchRequests","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedRequest","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/SkippedRecord"]},{"anchor":"Retrying-a-vendors-own-statuses","title":"Retrying a vendor’s own statuses","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/TransientStatus","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/InvalidTransientStatus"]},{"anchor":"Waiting-between-attempts","title":"Waiting between attempts","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/InvalidBackoff","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/NonPositiveRetry"]},{"anchor":"Sending-requests","title":"Sending requests","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/URLSessionTransport","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransportError"]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/httpdestinations"]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/TransientStatus":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TransientStatus","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A failure status that "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" retries, beside 408 Request Timeout, 429 Too Many"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Requests and every 5xx, for an encoder that lists it in "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder\/transientStatuses","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"title":"TransientStatus","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/transientstatus","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TransientStatus","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/TransientStatus","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/ResponseOutcome/rejected(reason:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome\/rejected(reason:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The vendor stored none of the request’s records, and wouldn’t if it were sent again, for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"reason","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the vendor’s own words where its body has them: "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" drops the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request and reports it as "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport\/rejectedInBody(status:reason:recordIDs:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/responseoutcome\/rejected(reason:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"rejected"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"reason"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"title":"ResponseOutcome.rejected(reason:)","kind":"symbol"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/InvalidTransientStatus":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"InvalidTransientStatus","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"InvalidTransientStatus","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/InvalidTransientStatus","type":"topic","title":"InvalidTransientStatus","abstract":[{"text":"The error ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/TransientStatus\/init(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" throws for a status that is neither a client error","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(4xx) nor a server error (5xx).","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/invalidtransientstatus"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchRequests":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BatchRequests"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchRequests","abstract":[{"text":"A batch as ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" encodes it: the requests that carry its records, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the records it left out.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"BatchRequests","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/batchrequests","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BatchRequests"}]},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/HTTPTransportResponse":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransportResponse","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"HTTPTransportResponse","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPTransportResponse","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/httptransportresponse","abstract":[{"text":"What an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" received for a request: the response’s status and header fields, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its body.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"HTTPTransportResponse"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/EncodedRequest/deadline":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedRequest\/deadline","abstract":[{"text":"The latest wall-clock time at which the request may be sent, or ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when it may be sent","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at any time.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"deadline","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/encodedrequest\/deadline","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"deadline","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Date","preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials4DateV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/dropReports":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/dropReports","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A report of each batch dropped without being delivered, in the order they are dropped."}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/dropreports","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dropReports","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncQueue","preciseIdentifier":"s:11AsyncQueues0A5QueueV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPDropReport","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations14HTTPDropReportO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Encoding","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Failure","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations12BatchEncoderP7FailureQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">>","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"dropReports"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchEncoder/outcome(of:for:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder\/outcome(of:for:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What the successful (2xx) answer "},{"code":"response","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"code":"request","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", one of this encoder’s requests,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"means: whether the vendor stored the request’s records."}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/batchencoder\/outcome(of:for:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","required":true,"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"outcome"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"of"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"HTTPTransportResponse","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations21HTTPTransportResponseV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"for"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"EncodedRequest","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations14EncodedRequestV"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ResponseOutcome","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15ResponseOutcomeO"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"outcome(of:for:)"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDropReport":{"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/httpdropreport","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport","role":"symbol","title":"HTTPDropReport","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPDropReport","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A batch "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" dropped without delivering it, and why."}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"HTTPDropReport","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://HTTPDesti